 
leetcode ques no 75. sort colors (optimal approach)
Given an array nums with n objects colored red, white, or blue, sort them in-place so that objects of the same color are adjacent, with the colors in the order red, white, and blue.

We will use the integers 0, 1, and 2 to represent the color red, white, and blue, respectively.

easy way to approach:
in this question colors of red,white,blue as 0,1,2 as numbers respectively;
initalize red ->0 and white ->0 and blue ->n-1;
using while loop check white never goes above the blue;
if its true then enter into if condition check the number is equal to 0;
if gets true then swap ele with red,whiteand increment red,white;
if gets false enter into anthor if condition check white =1;
then gets true increment white;
if get false swap ele with white,blue and decrement blue;


here is the pseudo code for this ques:
 void sortColors(vector<int>& nums) {
         
        int n=nums.size();
        int red=0;int white=0; int blue=n-1;
        while(white<=blue){
            if(nums[white]==0){
                swap(nums[white],nums[red]);
                red++;
                white++;

            }
            else if(nums[white]==1){
                white++;

            }
            else{
                swap(nums[white],nums[blue]);
                blue--;
            }
        }

time complexity:O(N);
its traversing whole array once;
space complexity:O(1)
there is no special memory i.e no required of any array to store elements for this problem.
